true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1816885419", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Dianna+Lopez+Meadow+Spirit&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2025 888"]}, {"t": 20688, "time": "05:44:48", "artist": "Worlds Only", "title": "Raw and hot", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Worlds+Only+Raw+and+hot", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Worlds+Only+Raw+and+hot", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Worlds+Only+Raw+and+hot", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Worlds+Only+Raw+and+hot", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1892955706", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Worlds+Only+Raw+and+hot", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Worlds+Only+Raw+and+hot&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2025 Worlds Only World"]}], "counts": {"high": 0, "mid": 23, "low": 9}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:33:53", "end": "00:34:54", "text": "Satsang with Mooji We are a leader. We are a leader."}, {"start": "00:35:02", "end": "00:35:48", "text": "The first three letters in Ngu means inner, Ngu means emotional. That's the definition of home for Wal-Pi people and Central Australian people. Ngu-ra, something that runs like a power source that keeps your body going. And that's your old Ngu-ra-kul history, your language history, your sermon history, your skin name ceremony, and your law within that tribe. Your jurisdiction."}, {"start": "00:36:18", "end": "00:36:55", "text": "To exist in the homeland of the kangaroo, you have to understand the emu. To understand it, we'll try and teach you to soar really high like the wet stand. It's like reading a book, text. The behavior of animals, the behavior of change of character."}, {"start": "00:37:06", "end": "00:38:30", "text": "It's just a law from this country. It shapes us who we are. They call this crown land. I sometimes wonder what crown. asks you to find out the original ground of this country. In doing that, you are like a milvery, fulfilling your duty of care, we'll call it. Ground is all because you've fulfilled something. Your fulfillment of caring your country, giving back to your country. And that's all the knowledge for your own well-being from this country, to give it back to people. In doing so, you already got the original crown. The emus crown."}, {"start": "00:38:42", "end": "00:40:21", "text": "The original crown is the Southern Cross here, because it's sitting on the emu's head. To us, that's the whole murakulu. It's a reminder that we mustn't be like a little star drifting away. That's why the little stars is the homeland. or this continent and to learn all Darwan will expand your learning how you should live in this country and firstly you must learn all these archives in the whole the law the skin name, the land the ceremony and the language To live in the Omna and the kangaroo, you have to understand the EMU."}, {"start": "00:40:34", "end": "00:41:26", "text": "Your country will know you. I am a man. I am a man. I am a man."}, {"start": "04:04:08", "end": "04:04:32", "text": ""}, {"start": "04:50:52", "end": "04:51:32", "text": "Satsang with Mooji women dance, flicking their finger like that. So they get to expand the light going this way horizontally."}, {"start": "04:52:00", "end": "04:52:48", "text": "First, it has to grow like a tree, straight up. That means, yeah, everything is born unto you. Everything around you, yeah, gonna be you. Embrace them while you can. Learn about them, because they'll guide you how you should live. Because you're gonna have to adapt to this harsh country and enjoy its richness, I guess, with that knowledge. Because if you don't, your birch ride is stripped from you and your life falls short. It's a really hard country out here."}, {"start": "04:54:29", "end": "04:55:15", "text": "Learning through these knowledges, through the initiation ceremony of this place here, that's what I mean by negative and positive consequences of the law. It makes or breaks you, Haka and Albert, it's just the way the country is built. or created, that's all."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:09:07"}, "track": {"title": "Deep Umbel", "artists": [{"name": "Troth"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:34:00"}, "track": {"title": "NGURRA KURLU (HOME)", "artists": [{"name": "Crown and Country"}, {"name": "Jerry Jangala Patrick"}, {"name": "MWNCI & Wanta Jampijinpa Pawu-Kurlpurlurnu"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:42:00"}, "track": {"title": "Jumpin Original", "artists": [{"name": "Todd Terry"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:43:00"}, "track": {"title": "I Want C & B to Fix My Car", "artists": [{"name": "Boof"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:44:00"}, "track": {"title": "Believe in Yourself (DJ Mixon and DJ Sveta Remix)", "artists": [{"name": "Vladimir Svetsky"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:49:29"}, "track": {"title": "Bush Honey (guku) [feat. Peter Knight, Aviva Endean 